# D4 — panfrost7580 render-only driver (integration test build).
# Apply ON TOP of d0-m1-minimal.fragment (M1 state stands: vendor fbdev
# keeps the panel, stock dt.img is never rebuilt, no display-driver swap).
# Enables ONLY the new CONFIG_DRM_PANFROST7580 driver (tristate, default n
# in drivers/gpu/drm/panfrost7580/Kconfig). Deps already closed by
# stock/M1: CONFIG_DRM=y, CONFIG_OF=y, CONFIG_DMA_SHARED_BUFFER=y;
# CONFIG_DRM_GEM_CMA_HELPER (bool, depends on DRM) is select'ed by the
# driver symbol itself. Deliberately NOT selected: DRM_KMS_HELPER (render
# only, no modeset helpers), PM_DEVFREQ/THERMAL (devfreq hook is a stub;
# OPP table is static in C per docs/reports/gpu31-dt.md section 4).
# =y (built-in) so there is no module/ramdisk install step: the candidate
# boot.img carries the driver. =m is equally supported by
# drivers/gpu/drm/panfrost7580/Makefile (deferred follow-up, needs
# modules_install into ramdisk-new.gz).
CONFIG_DRM_PANFROST7580=y
